# DROP IT — deploy-machine secrets + target for the PROD host.
#
# COPY to deploy/prod/.env.local (gitignored) and fill in. This is the ONLY
# place on the workstation where the host root password and the generated
# runtime secrets are allowed to live. Nothing here is ever committed.
#
#   cp deploy/prod/.env.example deploy/prod/.env.local
#   chmod 600 deploy/prod/.env.local
#   $EDITOR deploy/prod/.env.local
#
# deploy/prod/provision.sh resolves this file automatically ($PWD/deploy/prod/.env.local
# or next to the script), exports it, and uses it to:
#   * render /srv/dropit/etc/dropit.env from deploy/prod/systemd/dropit.env.example
#     (substituting __DB_PASSWORD__, __JWT_SECRET__, __TOTP_KEY__);
#   * set the same password on the Postgres role via ALTER ROLE, so the env file
#     and the database cannot drift apart.
#
# Generating the secrets (run from the repo root):
#   openssl rand -hex 32   # -> DROPIT_DB_PASSWORD (alphanumeric-safe: use tr -dc 'A-Za-z0-9')
#   openssl rand -hex 48   # -> DROPIT_JWT_SECRET
#   openssl rand -hex 32   # -> DROPIT_TOTP_KEY (exactly 32 bytes => AES-256-GCM)
#
# provision.sh generates any missing value itself and writes it back into
# .env.local, so a bare `cp` + edit of PROD_HOST/DROPIT_SSH_PASS is enough.
#
# This file is sourced by bash: KEY=value, no spaces around '=', no quoting
# needed for the values below (they are all shell-safe alphabets).

# --- connection to the target ----------------------------------------------
# SSH is password auth as root on this box; there is no key installed.
PROD_HOST=root@150.241.68.57
# Root password. Used only through the askpass helper (see deploy/prod/lib.sh):
# it is exported as DROPIT_SSH_PASS and never appears in argv or in a file on
# the target. Leave empty if you have installed an SSH key for this host.
DROPIT_SSH_PASS=

# --- generated runtime secrets ---------------------------------------------
# Postgres password for role `dropit`. Must match /srv/dropit/etc/dropit.env.
DROPIT_DB_PASSWORD=
# JWT signing secret.
DROPIT_JWT_SECRET=
# TOTP encryption key, exactly 32 bytes hex (64 chars).
DROPIT_TOTP_KEY=

# --- optional overrides -----------------------------------------------------
# Path to the askpass helper used for password auth. Defaults to
# ${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/dsh-ssh/askpass.sh, then falls back to an inline temp helper
# that lib.sh creates if the file is missing.
# SSH_ASKPASS=/tmp/dsh-ssh/askpass.sh
#
# Extra ssh options, e.g. a jump host.
# DEPLOY_SSH_EXTRA_OPTS="-o ProxyJump=bastion"